<%# The question list, from site_faq_entries in this locale.

  THE SAME ROWS THE STRUCTURED DATA IS BUILT FROM. W5's FAQPage JSON-LD reads these rows, not a copy, so the
  markup and the structured data cannot disagree -- which is both Google's own requirement and the honest
  arrangement.

  A link whose page is unpublished resolves to nil and is not rendered, so an answer never points at a 404.

  A QUESTION IS AN ITEM UNDER THE BLOCK'S OWN HEADING, SO IT IS SET LIKE ONE. The `dt` was `text-lg` -- the
  size this layout gives a page standfirst -- which made twelve questions compete with the H2 above them, and
  the `dd` declared no size at all, so an answer inherited the root 16px and ran the full width of a
  `max-w-6xl` article with no measure.

  TWO COLUMNS, BECAUSE THERE ARE TWELVE OF THEM. A single column of question and answer ran the length of a
  screen and a half with the outer half of the window empty beside it. The measure that matters is the
  answer's, and it is set on the column rather than on the page.
%>
<% entries = SiteFaqEntry.published_for(marketing_locale) %>
<% if entries.any? %>
  <%# The FAQPage node, from the SAME rows rendered below -- not a copy and not a summary. %>
  <% content_for :structured_data do %>
    <%= marketing_structured_data(marketing_faq_schema(entries)) %>
  <% end %>
  <section class="<%= tone %>">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
      <%= render 'marketing/shared/section_head', heading: section['heading'], lede: nil %>
      <dl class="mt-12 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-9 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <% entries.each do |entry| %>
          <% href = entry.link? ? marketing_target_href(entry.target) : nil %>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-lg font-semibold leading-[1.45] text-lyn-ink"><%= entry.question %></dt>
            <dd class="mt-2.5 text-base leading-[1.8] text-lyn-ink-soft">
              <p><%= entry.answer %></p>
              <%# The answer is its own paragraph so the link below it is a target rather than the last words
                of a sentence: it keeps its own line, reaches the 44px tap floor, and takes a focus ring, none
                of which a bare inline anchor inside the `dd` did. Same label treatment as a card's link. %>
              <% if href.present? %>
                <a class="mt-1 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-sm font-semibold text-lyn-royal transition-colors hover:text-lyn-ink focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue"
                   href="<%= href %>">
                  <%= entry.link_label %>
                </a>
              <% end %>
            </dd>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
<% end %>
